    {
      "label": "results",
      "html": "<p>&gt; The estimated material cost: ~$12-18. Molds estimated ~$15,000 – 25,000 (given by onsite machinist) for both shell halves, at over 1,000 units this brings enclosure cost to under $2 per unit. Reached &lt;$20 Target.</p><p>&gt; Alternative lab grade lysis equipment cost: $3,000 – 8,000 per unit, the handheld pipette reduces per deployment cost for the Department of Defense by 99%.</p><p>&gt; shot size ≤20 cm³ per half, 18.6 cm³</p><p>&gt; Materials used: polycarb, 316SS and platinum cure 60A meets ISO 10993 biocompatibility.</p>"
